PROJECT-SPECIFIC CONTEXT FOR GOTRANSIT:

The gotransit repository is a Next.js-based checkout and transit information system. 
When working in this codebase, note:

- The primary checkout surface is at src/components/pages/CheckoutPage, which contains 
  form validation logic including email field handling in CheckoutForm.tsx around line 307.
- Tests are executed via `npm run test` using Jest. A separate coverage check runs 
  `npm run test:coverage-check` which depends on `npm run build:config` as a pretest step 
  (see package.json scripts).
- All commits must pass the pre-commit hook defined in .husky/pre-commit, which runs 
  `npx lint-staged` and enforces branch naming: the branch name must match the pattern 
  `^(feature|bugfix|tech|release|hotfix)/[a-zA-Z0-9.-]+(/[a-z0-9-]+)?$`. Tickets 
  tagged "bugfix" should use a branch like `bugfix/AMSD-XXXX` or `bugfix/AMSD-XXXX/description`.
- Form validation is a core concern in this repository; changes to validation logic 
  (such as case-sensitivity rules for email confirmation) require corresponding test coverage.

